{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/245495-using-scion-stunts-in-combat-house-rules","id":245495,"title":"Using Scion Stunts in Combat House Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-31T11:27:34-07:00","id":245495,"title":"Using Scion Stunts in Combat House Rules","content":"What are your thoughts on making the following House Rule workable? We're trying to encourage combat that is more cinematic, particularly like the Matrix movies.<br /> <br /> Stunts: in combat, player characters (and significant antagonists) can gain from 1-3 extra dice on ANY roll (including Dodge) by providing descriptions to their actions. Stunts should include cinematic, barely-realistic descriptions, interactions with the environment, improbable coincidences, and character flair. Particularly flat, bland, rote declarations of actions incur a -1 penalty. Stunts are limited to a 1 die bonus to powers that already provide a 3 die or more bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T12:45:07-07:00","id":245586,"title":"","content":"If someone's not feeling comfortable with the idea of stunting there shouldn't be a penalty beyond not getting a bonus. This just makes them feel worse for not being out there with their stunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDef